WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations
on season three of the show.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.402 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are a co-creator
of this show.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're the showrunner
of this show.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am.
-You're also in it.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:09.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are scenes
where you have fights.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-There are fires.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is nudity for yourself.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:15.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you ever regret,
once you start shooting it,

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you made yourself
do those things?

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have no one to blame
but myself.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's not just fire.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
I lit myself on fire.
-Yeah.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which turns out is hot.
-Yeah.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, that's, like, the --
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.063
-It's like the key thing.
Everybody knows about fire.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I didn't.
I didn't know that.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughing ]

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.835
-Especially when I say, "Can
you put more gasoline on me?"

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, it gets really hot.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And is it something like,
in the moment,

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're actually
now on fire, do you think back

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.377
to the writers room
and the moment where it came up

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that you didn't
spike it then?

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:46.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, of course.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's when you think --
-Yeah.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.684
There was one moment
I was actually on a snowmobile.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.887
I did this jump on a snowmobile
into a river,

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then it goes
down in the river,

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.257 size:81% position:41%
and these safety guys
come up to me and say,

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:59.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know, the worst that's
gonna happen is, like,

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
the snowmobile, like,
rolls over on you

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're pinned for
like a minute."

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:04.631 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:05.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know, but we'll be there.
We'll be there.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can hold your breath
for a minute, right?"

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is so much worse.
-Like, "No!"

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the worst
I thought could happen.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:14.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-So, you co-created this show

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
with your wife, Sam Bee.
-Yes.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who's also very talented.
And you guys have kids.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
And your kids have gotten
to be in episodes.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
They don't play your children
in the show,

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they got to be
sort of extras.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:24.551 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Did they enjoy it?

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, my son
was, like, a featured actor.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.154
-Oh, great!
-He plays young me on the show.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:31.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, fantastic!
-And my daughters were extras.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I cut them.
-Oh, wow.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Now, that's -- that's rough.

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know!
-That's rough to begin with,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.467
but then, with your son having a
plum role, that's really rough.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And his paycheck is giant,
and theirs is nothing.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
So how do you have to --

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you tell your kids
they're cut?

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.276 size:78% position:39%
-I was like, "Listen,
your scene was good."

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"It wasn't great."

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-But I gave them a scene --

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:57.951
I actually gave them a speaking
role in the next season.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:58.918 line:92%
That was season one I cut them.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
Season two,
I gave them a speaking role.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:04.858
And they were mad at me because
they liked their part better

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the first season.
-Oh, no!

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.061 line:92%
-I'm like, "You get paid now!

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did it for free
as an extra."

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.632 size:78% position:39%
-But they have taste.
-Now you get paid.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They didn't care
for the new scene.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:16.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-You're obviously a writer.

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're an actor,
you're a comedian.

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.473
-Yes.
-Don't take this the wrong way.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.842
I would not have guessed
that you began in modeling.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:25.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you had
an early modeling career.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:25.979 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're suggesting
that I'm an ugly child.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.383 size:81% position:41%
-No, I'm not at all!
-And you're not wrong!

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:33.219
-No.
How did modeling start for you?

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:37.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It started
like any child model.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:39.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
My grandmother
owned a bridal boutique.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
Perfect!

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:43.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they're like,
"He can fit into a dress!"

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.631 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:47.500
Yeah.
-You actually sent some photos.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-This is not bridal work.

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:51.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
This is my later work.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Later work.
So this is pretty --

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:55.241 size:75% position:38%
I mean, this is rad,
and that's the word

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
we used then
to describe that look.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
-So, what is the brand here

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you're...?
-I don't -- Leather pants?

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I don't know.

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.450 size:81% position:41%
Well, there's a story.
Because show this one.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, this one is fantastic.
-This one.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.956
-I mean, that's fantastic.
-Well, it's not fantastic.

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.992
Because he was not a great
Michael Jackson impersonator.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-And I was really mad

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:18.498 size:81% position:41%
that I had to just sit
on the bench and snap.

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.065 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Interesting.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.568
-'Cause I could do the Moonwalk
way better than him.

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:25.271 size:88% position:44%
And I didn't understand
at the time, as a child,

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
that maybe me
playing Michael Jackson

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
is probably not
the best casting choice.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:32.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
That if you were
opening a catalogue

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:35.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they went with you
instead of the other kid...

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, funny story.
I meet this kid again

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
on a casting call,
a go-see, I guess --

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
A go-see.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a little modeling
lingo for you.

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:45.358 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I meet him again,
and we're both up

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:51.297 line:92%
for this department-store shoot.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:54.000
It's called Robinsons, which is,
like, the Gimbels of Canada.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.973
And we were up for the role
of Mr. T for a Halloween shoot.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.342 size:78% position:39%
And guess who got it.
-You booked Mr. T?!

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I booked Mr. T.
-Oh, my God.

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't clap for that!
-Yeah.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:10.083
-I shouldn't have booked Mr. T!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because it was
a short-sleeve outfit,

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they didn't give me
a shirt to wear.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it just a black mask
with white arms.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:17.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:20.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And a sign that said Mr. T
on the plastic outfit.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is rough.
That really speaks volumes

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:25.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
about how bad this guy
was at impressions.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:28.368 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He didn't even have to talk.
-Yeah.

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:31.804 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I know. Yeah.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's who I pity.
I pity him.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You pity him!
I pity him!

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:37.143 size:84% position:42%
-Thanks for being here.
Congrats on the show.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
Always a pleasure
to see you, man.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:43.016
Jason Jones, "The Detour,"
airs Tuesday nights on TBS.

